1 against AC-1.1 through AC-1.4, including the Convex archive entry mutation/query, schema and PlatformStore wiring, shared archive contracts, documented TC mappings, the local test harness, and the configured story/epic gates.\",\"priorFindingStatuses\":[],\"newFindings\":[{\"id\":\"S1-F1\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Story 1 scope and evidence requirements conflict, leaving AC-1.1 and AC-1.4 unproven\",\"evidence\":\"The story scope explicitly defers live finalization hooks, archive read routes/UI, and read-time provenance enrichment to later stories (`docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/01-canonical-archive-entry-persistence.md:36-38`, `174-178`), but the same story still requires TC-1.1a/b/c and TC-1.4a/b coverage (`.../01-canonical-archive-entry-persistence.md:156-166`, `192-199`; `docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/test-plan.md:36-44`). Those mapped files do not exist (`tests/service/server/archive-finalization.test.ts`, `tests/service/server/archive-api.test.ts`), `rg` found no `ArchiveFinalizationService`/`appendFinalizedEntry` or `ArchiveReadService`/`getArchive` implementation under `apps/platform/server/services`, and the only executable proof is the Convex handler test (`convex/archiveEntries.test.ts:196-236`, `370-436`). That leaves finalized user/model/process-event archival and degraded related-context reads without the required story-level evidence.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/01-canonical-archive-entry-persistence.md\",\"docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/test-plan.md\",\"convex/archiveEntries.test.ts\",\"tests/service/server/archive-finalization.test.ts\",\"tests/service/server/archive-api.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-1.1\",\"TC-1.1a\",\"TC-1.1b\",\"TC-1.1c\",\"AC-1.4\",\"TC-1.4a\",\"TC-1.4b\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"human-ruling\",\"blocking\":true},{\"id\":\"S1-F2\",\"severity\":\"minor\",\"title\":\"The production archive read path paginates after loading the full process archive\",\"evidence\":\"`listArchiveEntries` reads `by_processId_and_sequence` with `.collect()` and only then slices in `paginateArchiveEntries` (`convex/archiveEntries.ts:139-155`, `261-280`). The story/design describe this store method as returning one bounded page (`docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/01-canonical-archive-entry-persistence.md:126-127`; `docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:661-668`). The outward page contract is correct, but long-process production reads still materialize the full archive in memory.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"convex/archiveEntries.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-1.3\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"quick-fix\",\"blocking\":false}],\"openFindings\":[{\"id\":\"S1-F1\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Story 1 scope and evidence requirements conflict, leaving AC-1.1 and AC-1.4 unproven\",\"evidence\":\"The story scope explicitly defers live finalization hooks, archive read routes/UI, and read-time provenance enrichment to later stories (`docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/01-canonical-archive-entry-persistence.md:36-38`, `174-178`), but the same story still requires TC-1.1a/b/c and TC-1.4a/b coverage (`.../01-canonical-archive-entry-persistence.md:156-166`, `192-199`; `docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/test-plan.md:36-44`). Those mapped files do not exist (`tests/service/server/archive-finalization.test.ts`, `tests/service/server/archive-api.test.ts`), `rg` found no `ArchiveFinalizationService`/`appendFinalizedEntry` or `ArchiveReadService`/`getArchive` implementation under `apps/platform/server/services`, and the only executable proof is the Convex handler test (`convex/archiveEntries.test.ts:196-236`, `370-436`). That leaves finalized user/model/process-event archival and degraded related-context reads without the required story-level evidence.\",\"affectedFiles\