{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_42","type":"agent_message","text":"Updated the real Convex archive read path in [convex/archiveEntries.ts](/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/convex/archiveEntries.ts:139) so `listArchiveEntries` now does a single indexed range read for the requested `processId`, optional exclusive `cursor`, and `limit`, then uses a one-row lookahead via `.take(limit + 1)` to preserve the existing `hasMore` and `nextCursor` semantics. The response contract, ascending `sequence` order, and cursor behavior stay the same; the only behavioral change is that we no longer `.collect()` the full archive before slicing.\n\nI also updated the in-memory Convex test harness in [convex/test_helpers/fake_convex_context.ts](/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/convex/test_helpers/fake_convex_context.ts:9) to support `gt/gte/lt/lte` index ranges and proper numeric comparison, so the archive unit tests still exercise the same query shape production now uses.\n\nVerified with:\n- `pnpm vitest run convex/archiveEntries.test.ts tests/service/server/archive-api.test.ts`\n- `pnpm vitest run tests/service/client/archive-section.test.ts`\n- `pnpm run red-verify`"}}
